category: Convenience and Electrical
platform: Ranger (6G)
model_years: 2024+
trim: All
validated: true
verified_by: Kyle / AsBuiltPro
source_sheet: (2024+) 6G Ranger.xlsx
notes: '0001=1 second.  convert decimal value to hex.   For example 3600 seconds equates
  to 0E10, and 1800 seconds is 0708

  FORScan Menu: Power Point Timeout, s (Set to # of seconds desired (e.g. 1800 for
  30 minutes))

  Trim: All [Confirmed: craigc (9/16/2024) Lariat]

  DeltaNu1142''s power point timeout calculator'
forscan_menu: 'Power Point Timeout, s (Set to # of seconds desired (e.g. 1800 for
  30 minutes))'
steps:
- module: BCM
  address: 726-57-01
  mask: '**** xxxx xx--'
  notes: 'User input required: Enter timeout duration in seconds converted to hex
    (e.g. 0E10 = 3600s / 1hr; factory default is 1194 = 4500s / 75 min). Keep factory
    value unless customizing.'
  type: continuous
  unit: seconds
  feature_name: Power_Point_Maxtime_Cfg (PPMC)
  instruction: 0001=1 second.  convert decimal value to hex.   For example 3600 seconds
    equates to 0E10, and 1800 seconds is 0708
  user_input: required
